{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jacob dwelt.</b> It connects to 'Esau dwelt in Mount Seir' — after it told you how Esau settled in Mount Seir, it went back and wrote that Jacob dwelt <b>in the land of the sojournings of his father</b>, for the right of the firstborn is his, since he acquired it for money, and his due is to inherit his father's estate, and Esau went his way like a stranger." "<b>In the land of the sojournings of his father, in the land of Canaan.</b> Both are needed. If it did not say 'in the land of the sojournings of his father,' we would not know in which city. And if it did not say 'in the land of Canaan,' I would say 'the land of the sojournings of his father' — that is Abraham, and that would be Ur of the Chaldees." "<b>And Jacob dwelt in the land of the sojournings of his father.</b> It writes this to inform you that the word of HaShem endures forever, for He said to Abraham, 'and I will give to you and to your seed after you the land of your sojournings.' For the patriarchs too settled in it: of Abraham it says, 'and he dwelt in the terebinths of Mamre, which is in Hebron'; of Isaac it says, 'and Isaac sowed in that land'; of Jacob it says, 'and Jacob dwelt in the land of the sojournings of his father.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:39.231574896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}